37890	38076	37872	37872	she	103	" They are gone to pray for a fine harvest , and that she wants herself as well -- it costs seven francs apiece . They take their food with them ; they go and laugh and eat in the fields . I think it is nonsense . One can say one 's prayers just as well here . Mère Krebs thinks so too , but then she says , ' If I do not go , it will look ill ; people will say I am irreligious ; and as we make so much by flour , God would think it odd for me to be absent ; and , besides , it is only seven francs there and back ; and if it does please Heaven , that is cheap , you know . One will get it over and over again in Paradise . ' That is what Mere Krebs says . But , for me , I think it is nonsense . It can not please God to go by train and eat galette and waste a whole day in getting dusty .
